Date: October 22, 2026
System: Proxmox VE 9 / Debian 13 (Trixie)
Status: Resolved
Overview
While preparing Voyager for Tailscale, I ran into package installation errors. APT could not refresh its package lists because some configured repositories were unavailable or incorrect.
Investigation
The update output included 401 Unauthorized errors from Proxmox enterprise repositories and 404 Not Found errors from an incorrect Debian security repository URL. Editing /etc/apt/sources.list alone did not solve the problem because additional repository definitions were still present under /etc/apt/sources.list.d/, including .sources files.
Resolution
I inspected the active repository definitions, backed up the configuration, removed or corrected conflicting entries, and configured the appropriate Debian and Proxmox no-subscription repositories. I then refreshed APT and installed the tools needed for the Tailscale setup.

Useful verification commands:
apt-get clean
apt-get update
apt-get install -y curl
Outcome
apt-get update completed successfully, and I was able to continue installing Tailscale. No reinstall of Proxmox was needed.
Lessons learned
- APT reads repository definitions from both sources.list and sources.list.d/.
- HTTP errors help narrow the issue: 401 suggests an authorization problem; 404 indicates the requested resource was not found.
- Back up configuration files and inspect all active sources before changing repositories.
